From ada407df4c57413bb6c7c8f3bb4c29803cb394fe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jeffrey <jeffrey@SparkThree.vpn.dk>
Date: Sat, 16 May 2026 11:30:27 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] fork: Section 6 - Streaming production cache for models
 too large for CUDA

Qwen3-Coder-Next (79.67B params, ~159 GB BF16) exceeds the GB10 Grace-Blackwell's
121.63 GB CUDA-visible UMA. AutoModelForCausalLM.from_pretrained triggers
caching_allocator_warmup which allocates 120.43 GiB in a single fp16 tensor;
118.94 GiB were free -> OOM.

_estimate_model_bytes_from_index(): reads total_size from
model.safetensors.index.json; falls back to single-shard file size.

_fill_production_cache_streaming(): reuses _build_streaming_context /
_call_layer infrastructure (same as Fisher probe). Per layer: install ->
run all N calibration samples -> compute NVFP4 joint globals -> render GPTQ
weights -> unload. Peak CUDA: ~4 GB (one layer) + 134 MB (hidden states).

main(): auto-routes to streaming path when model_bytes > cuda_total - 4 GB;
adds --halo-mode/--halo-seed argparse args (lost in upstream merge) and
AutoConfig import for HALO non-streaming path.

Limitations: HALO, recache, AWQ, SmoothQuant, fisher passes are unsupported
in the streaming path (all require full model resident).
